learning='''<section class="learning wrap" id="learning"><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCHERS · MAKERS · CURIOUS MINDS</p><h2>Learn With Hemp.</h2><p>Bring a question, a research focus or an idea for a small group. We are developing focused sessions around natural materials and everyday uses of hemp.</p><div class="hemp-path-grid"><article><h3>Natural building</h3><p>Discuss a materials demonstration or introduction to hempcrete and finishes, with scope and facilitation agreed in advance.</p></article><article><h3>Farm to material</h3><p>Future seasonal sessions may follow cultivation and processing as the on-site patch develops. These activities are not currently guaranteed.</p></article><article><h3>Make &amp; discover</h3><p>Register interest in proposed hemp-soap or hemp-food sessions. Each session will be announced only once its facilitator, materials and arrangements are confirmed.</p></article></div><p class="small-print">No fixed workshop calendar is open yet. Dates, facilitator, group size, materials, fees and inclusions must be confirmed before payment. Research visits require an agreed scope; group sessions are planned around the quiet of the house and village.</p>'''+enquiry_link('Hello, I would like to discuss a Learn With Hemp visit. My topic, dates, group size and learning goals are:','Discuss a learning visit ↗')+'</section>'
body=pages['retreats'][1]
body=body.replace('START A RETREAT CONVERSATION','PLAN A WORKSHOP OR RETREAT').replace('Start a retreat conversation.','Plan a workshop or retreat.').replace('<option>Architecture & natural building</option>','<option>Architecture & natural building</option><option>Builder trial stay</option><option>Hemp materials workshop</option><option>Research residency</option><option>Future farm / soap / food session</option>')
pages['retreats']=('Workshops & Retreats',learning+body)
pages['story']=(pages['story'][0],pages['story'][1]+section('THE NEXT CHAPTER','An ancestral home.<br>A living hemp story.','Gaurav and Namrata’s next chapter connects the home with a small planned cultivation patch and a dedicated Hemp Experience Center. The intention is to make hemp tangible—from plant and material to the experience of living with it—while respecting the calm and traditions of the village.'))
